** Introduction

ASPEN.K2 provides GPU/CUDA users with automatic-tuned high performance
Level2 BLAS kernels. ASPEN.K2 comes from a shortened name of
`Automatic Stabilizing and PEformance tuNing of level 2 BLAS Kernels.'

ASPEN.K2 is Open Source Software (OSS).
See the copyright form 'LICENCE.txt'.



** Prerequisite **
   CUDA:: SDK 13.x later
   CC: GCC or Intel OneAPI
   PYTHON:: version 3, aliased to python or python3, and numpy, scipy, and cxxfilt
   BLAS:: OpenBLAS or Intel MKL

** Getting started.

 0) You are supposed to be at the directory 'ASPEN.K2[-(version)]/',
    where you got extracted the tarball, and set up two environment
    variables, $CUDA_PATH and $ASPEN_GPU_ID,
    correctly in advace of the following steps.
    $CUDA_PATH is the directory on which CUDA is installed, and
    $ASPEN_GPU_ID is optional and it specifies the GPU ID on which
    ASPEN.K2 will be tuned up.
 1) Modify src/Makefile appropriately.
 2) Do 'make' or 'make tuned'. Then, lib/libaspen.a is created.
    By default, the library is optimized for a GeForce GTX1080.
 3) Do 'make benchmark'. This yields benchmark programs in bench/.
 4) See include/aspen.h for available API's of ASPEN.K2.
 5) If you need the AT version which is optimized on your GPU environment,
    do 'make tuned-new'. This overwrites the libaspen.a by the auto-tuned
    version in lib/. However, fully tuning might take a day.
    If your GPU faciliates large GDDR, for example more than 10GB, you
    need a couple of days.
    Or, if you want to tune up only the specific routine 'XXXX',
    do 'make tuned-new-XXXX', XXXX refers to
    '([dswh]|i{16,32,64,128})symv(_[ul])' or '([kczu])hemv(_[ul])'.
    While the tuning process, two applications; Intel-MKL, python with numpy
    and scipy packages, are required to predict the performance.
    If compilation fails, please modify tuning/*.sh carefully.
 6) If you need to tune up again, do 'make tuned-new'
    or 'make tuned-new-XXXX'.

 ** CAUTION **
    Please do not use 'make -j', because concurrent make would
    access a GPU by multiple precesses simultaneously,
    and then violate intermediate data.



** Release information

Version 1.12:
Experimental support of CUDA 13.3. and Blackwell generations.
Replace "atom.add" by "red.add" to reduce the memory cycle pressure.
Use a strong "red.add" to avoid a racing among remote TBs.  
Tweak the ocuupancy calculation based on opt-in shared memory model.
Tweak on tuning script, which leverage the Paleto-optimul condition.
Static parametrization of the reduce_in_block kernels.
If exclusive ops are not neccessary, swich (by buffer=NULL) bewteen tickect and atom/red mode.
Experimental implementation of an asyncronous-grouop non-bulk copy by "cp.async" gmem -> smem.

Version 1.11:
Experimental support of CUDA 13.2, 13.1, 13.0, and 12.X.
and new HW generations of Ada, and Hopper, and Blackwell(GB120).
Obsolate the task control mechanism.
Introduce multi-ticket zoning algorithm, which may be categorized as a hybrid of mutex and scatter-and-gather algorithm.
Supporting to choose reproducible or non-reproducible atomic algorithm.
Introduced strong memory order mechanism, to mix up atomic operations.
__int128, which is alised int128 internally, has been adapted, while it was emulation by two int64_t's in the former versions.
Tweak on tuning scripts, which does not adapt our policies that
activate resource must be largest enough.
Debug on the occupancy calculation if CG > 800.
Rename include/<typename>.h into include/_<typename>.h to avoid filename conflict with system header files.

Version 1.10:
Fully switch the Confirmed store to the atomicAdd/pokeAdd.
Experimental support of CUDA 12.0, and 12.1, but not support of int128_t.
Obsolated the texture-type management on CUDA 12.0 later.
Parameters of AdaLovelace and Hopper are included, but not confirmed correct performances on them.
half dtatype is overridded thanks to the introduction of half.h,
which can emulate IEE754 FP16 compatible half precision on the host side.
Slightly modified the DD multiplication scheme.
Slightly modified ptx-inlines with a predicated condition.
Slightly modified nvcc options.

Version 1.9p1:
Experimental support of CUDA 11.7, and 11.8.
Slightly modified a few warp-diverged loops.

Version 1.9:
Experimental support of CUDA 11.6.
Thread Block sync model is modified, and adjusted for the A100 model, which does not fully activate MULT*numMP thread-blocks initially, also for avoidance of the re-entry from unexpected failures.
Simplified the kernel template, but also added L+U kernel again to improve performance for small size cases.
Reduced the division operations so that they are issued on the master thread and broadcasted via shared memory.
Slightly modified Store_with_confirmation to simplify the loop structure as a single form.
KHEMV (Komplex HEMV) kernel performing complex number based on the half precision (fp16 aka half) has been supported.
Half precision for GP10X compatibles is enabled, but very slow.
Fixed the internal-int64 casting for multiplications by int32 integer numbers.

Version 1.8p1:
Experimental support of CUDA 11.3, 11.3.1, 11.4, and 11.5.
Small revisions on this README.
Random sampling has been adapted to avoid lower-clock workload due to the unexpected mode transition around P8 to P2 states.
Tuning profiles on A100 (GA100), RTX-A5000, and RTX3090 (GA102), are included.

Version 1.8:
Support of CUDA 11.0, 11.1, and 11.2.
Support of integer SYMV kernels; i128symv, i64symv, i32symv, and i16symv.
Modify multi-regsiter accumulation functions summing along a warp.
Use atomicAdd for 32bit builtin ops with exclusive control to keep the bitwise reproducibility. 
Modify data-conversion mechanism by using 'reinterpret_cast<datatype *>'.
Tweak on a warmup mode, which may, however, not be so effective...
Introduce new data structures in aspen_const.h, aspen_d[df]{real|complex}.h and aspen_int{16,128}.h, referred to the CUDA SDK (cuda_fp16.h).
Tweak on a memory sychnorozation, which has been defined from sm70/PTX v6.0.
Experimental support of HSYMV
Experimental support of sm_80 and sm_86, so called Ampere series.

Version 1.7:
Support of CUDA 10.0, 10.1 and 10.2.
Experimental support of sm_75, Turing core
Respond to unexpected infinite-loops, which happned when exceptional NaNs due to the out-of-bound access or invalid region of the triangular matrix.
Unification of the source codes both in upper and lower.
Rewrite of some shell scripts into python.
Deprecated support on the old CUDA SDKs, such as 9.x or prior.

Version 1.6p4:
Volatile ld-st operations via shared memory among threads in a thread block.
Some updates and arranges for the header files.
Replace cudaThreadSyncronize() to cudaDeviceSynchronize().
Experimental support of sm_75, Turing core.

Version 1.6p3:
Support CUDA 9.1 and 9.2.
Support sm_70, Volta GV100 core (only confirmed on a TITAN-V).
Partly enchanced v2 or v4 accesses of vectors stored in shared memory.

Version 1.6p2:
Support CUDA 9.0.
Support stride parameter of the vectors x and y: ie. incx and incy.
Experimental support of sm_70, Volta GV100 core.
Tune up the vector accesses such as double2 and float[24].
Extend the sumup routine processing multiple registers,
specifically, from 8 upto 16 parameter registers.
Again, minor modification for the parameter search scripts.
Bug fix for the occupancy calculation in case of GP100.
Obsolate the old CUDA versions, such as 7.5 or prior.

Version 1.6p1:
Modify the get_mult command for sm_37, sm_53, and sm_6x.
Tune up the diagonal block kernel.
Minor modification for the parameter search scripts.
Exprimental support of CUDA 9.0.

Version 1.6:
Support the double-double format; wsymv and uhemv.
Support both static and shared library formats: libaspen.a and libaspen.so.
Support stream interface, ASPEN_setStream and ASPEN_getStream.
Unify symv and hemv templates into hesymv template.
Tune up the kernel by introducing internal fma2 and add2 operations.
Minor modification for the parametre search scripts.
Gemv kernels have been obsolated from this version.

Version 1.5p9:
Support Complex functions; zhemv and chemv.
Minor modification for the parametre search script of symv_reguse.sh
so as not to miss the candidate to be explored.

Version 1.5p8:
Modify the block-grid shape as a two-dimensional grid.
Simplify the compilation process which is done for each sm_(20,30,...).
Modify the Makefile rules to reduce the compliation time.
Exprimental support of CUDA 8.0 and pascal architectures (sm_(60,61,62)).
Exprimental support of half precision of Level1 BLAS.

Version 1.5p7:
Loop re-structured technique is employed for symv kernels.
Correct the capacity of the shared memory for the Maxwell architecture.
Tuning shell scripts is slightly changed so as to allow a wider-ranged
parameters space,
      max{32, BASE(=VX*m)} <= BLOCK_SIZE*VX <= 512,
      32 <= BLOCK_SIZE(=32*k) <= 256, 1<=VX<=8, and 1 <= BASE(=VX*m) <= 192.
      In addition, multiplicity >= 2.
Also user can choose whether rough and full search modes by the environment
variable ASPEN_TUNING_LEVEL. If ASPEN_TUNING_LEVEL equals to 'ROUGH' or
'FULL', the search mode is designated in rough search or Bruto-force search,
respectively. BUT, the ROUGH mode yields acceptable good result in most cases.
Introduce ASPEN_ERROR_CHECK to control the error check during tuning process.
Arrange the header files.
Implement a couple of Level 1 BLAS routines such as axpy, scal, etc.
Preliminary version of cu(Float|Double)complex for Level 1 BLAS.

Version 1.5p6:
Minor change for symv kernels.
Minor change for tuning shell scripts to reduce the number of parameter
samplings.
Support CUDA 7.5.

Version 1.5p5:
Minor change for symv kernels so as not to fall in deadlock.
Minor change for tuning shell scripts to reduce the number of parameter
samplings.

Version 1.5p4:
Minor change for symv kernels allowing wide-ranged parameters, especially
MULTIPLICITY=1 and BLOCK_SIZE*VX <= 512.
Minor change for reduction rountines.
Minor change for tuning shell scripts.
Reformat the source files by the indent mechanism of the emacs C++-mode.

Version 1.5p3:
Minor change for [ds]symv_l kernels to reduce the register consumption.
Obsolate the L+U algorithm adpopted in [ds]symv_u kernels.
Bug fix for [ds]gemv_n in case of non-square matrices.
Support both CUDA 7.0RC and CUDA 6.5 on which 'sm_52' is available.
Bug fix for the occupancy calculation in case of the Fermi architecture.

Version 1.5p2:
Bug fix for an infinite loop trap in [ds]symv_l kernels.
Minor change for [ds]symv_l kernels.
Invalidate the Tesla kernel implementations,
Modify Makefile and shell scripts not to use the deviceQuery command.

Version 1.5p1:
Modify [ds]symv_[lu] kernels to support the sumup routine via shared memory.

Version 1.5:
Add 'L'ower triangular matrix format for [ds]symv.
Modify tuning scripts of [ds]symv_[lu].sh to support full multiplicity upto
32 for the Maxwell architectures.

Version 1.4p1:
Experimental support for sm_50 (Maxwell aka GM107) and a brandnew architecture
refered to sm_52 (Maxwell2 aka GM204).
Minor bug fix for a script which generates if-then rules to switch parameters.
Minor change for SYMV kernel in oder to avoid deadlock.
Bug fix in the occupancy calculation for larger shared memory (32/48KB).
Rewrite Makefiles' rules.

Version 1.4:
Divide the Kepler codes into sm_30 (Kepler aka GK104) and sm_35 (Kepler2
aka GK106 later).
Minor bug fix in [ds]symv.sh and minor change in [ds]symv kernels.
Minor change in the searching algorithm for [ds]symv by 3-step algorithm.
Modify the primal Makefile and remove redundant source files.
Bug fix in the occupancy calculation for the Fermi architecture.

Version 1.3p1:
Minor bug fix.
From this version, ASPEN.K2 is released as Open Source Software.

Version 1.3:
Minor bug fix and vector2 load is newly applied for SYMV kernel.

Version 1.2:
New kernel implementation for SYMV is introduced.

Version 1.0:
The current release supports some of the Level 2 BLAS kernels
for the CUDA environment focused on the Fermi and Kepler architectures
with CUDA version 5.5 later.
(Maxwell architecture and CUDA prior to 5.0 are not officially supported.)
The first release supports [DS]GEMV, both operations for normal 'N or n'
and transposition 'T or t', [DS]SYMV, only for the upper ('U or u')
triangular format.



** Available functios

 1) {I{16,32,64,128},[DSWH]}SYMV, both the upper ('U or u') and the lower
    ('L or l') triangular matrix formats for a symmetric matrix ('L or l'
    is supported from version 1.5)
 2) [ZCUK]HEMV, both the upper ('U or u') and the lower ('L or l') triangular
    matrix formats for a hermite matrix (the lower triangular format,
    in short 'L or l', is supported from version 1.5, and the FP16 precision,
    'K', format is suppoted from 1.9)

 *) HSYMV kernel works on the most of GPU later than or same as Pascal.
 *) GEMV kernels are obsolated from version 1.6


